$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=lsfiberlem3  LOC_AFTER=?

* Lemma for lsfiber: inducing the inverse of a primitive character mod f up to level Q is an injection of the primitive characters mod f into the characters mod Q (Lean hinj at one level).

s1::simpl |- ( ( ( ( Q e. NN /\ M e. RR ) /\ ( W e. Fin /\ W C_ ZZ /\ A : W --> CC ) /\ A. m e. W ( m gcd Q ) = 1 ) /\ f e. { d e. NN | ( d || Q /\ ( ( mmu ` ( Q / d ) ) =/= 0 /\ ( ( Q / d ) gcd d ) = 1 ) ) } ) -> ( ( Q e. NN /\ M e. RR ) /\ ( W e. Fin /\ W C_ ZZ /\ A : W --> CC ) /\ A. m e. W ( m gcd Q ) = 1 ) )
